$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for Transformation of Oximes
into Amide and Nitriles. SOCl2 (6 mmol) was added dropwise to a solution
of oxime (5 mmol) in acetone (2 ml), with stirring at 0-10 °C. Then a
clear solution of β-CD (0.5 mmol) in distilled water (10 ml) was added at
room temperature and stirred at 80 °C for the appropriate time (monitored
by TLC). The organic material was extracted in ethyl acetate (3 × 20 ml).
The aqueous layer was cooed to 0 °C; in which β-CD reappeared as a white
solid. The obtained white solid mass was filtered, dried to recover β-CD,
and reused. The organic phase was dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, the
solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure, and the crude product
purified by column chromatography using hexane-ethyl acetate as eluent.
Entry: 4, Amide, Yield: 90%, Time: 20 min. A molar ratio of
ketoximes-SOCl2-β-CD = 5:6:0.5.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Beckmann rearrangement, catalyst recyclable
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM SOCl2/β-cyclodextrin: A new and efficient catalytic system for Beckmann
rearrangement and dehydration of aldoximes under aqueous condition
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Patil, Dipak; Dalal, Dipak
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2013), 43(1), 118-128

