$DATUM 1318-93-0
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Montmorillonite K 10 was dried and
simultaneously activated in a microwave oven for 3 min at 780 W prior to
use. In a typical experiment, the oxime (300 mg) was intimately mixed
with clay and the glass vessel (Pyrex) was irradiated in a domestic
microwave oven during the appropriated time at 780 W; after cooling, the
reaction mixture is washed with diethyl ether followed by filtration of
clay and removal of the solvent under reduced pressure and the products
were isolated and purified by crystallization. All amides and lactams
prepared are known compounds identified by physical properties (m.p., IR
and 1H-RMN) and compared with those of authentic samples. 1b, yield 91%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM montmorillonite K10 catalyst; microwaves
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Microwave assisted Beckman rearrangement of ketoximes in dry media
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Bosch, Ana I.; de la Cruz, Pilar; Diez-Barra, Enrique; Loupy, Andre;
Langa, Fernando
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (1995), (12), 1259-60

