$DATUM 7787-60-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Beckmann Rearrangement of oximes :-
Benzophenone oxime 1 (R=Ph, 10 mmol) and bismuth trichloride9 (12 mmol)
were mixed together in an Erlenmeyer flask and placed in a commercial
microwave oven (operating at 2450 MHz frequency) and irradiated for 8
minutes. The reaction mixture was allowed to reach room temperature,
treated with 20% sodium bicarbonate solution and extracted with
dichloromethane and dried over anhydrous sodium sulphate. Removal of
solvent and the residue on purification by column chromatography on
silica gel gave the corresponding benzanilide in 90% yield and there was
no evidence for. the formation of any deoximated products. Similar
treatment of 2-methyleyclohexanone and 1-tetralone oximes gave the
corresponding ring expanded rearranged products in 75-80% yields as
summerised in the table and their characteristics are recorded here. 2a,
yield 90%. mp 162°C, Lit 11 mp 162°C, 1H NMR 7.05-7.33 (m, 11H, ArH &
NH). IR (KBr); 3445, 1650 cm-1 . MS m/e; 197(M+). Anal. Calcd. (found)
for C13H11NO; C, 79.18 (79.26); H, 5.58 (5.66); N, 7.06 (7.12)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Microwave induced bismuth trichloride catalysed beckmann rearrangement of
oximes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
