$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Conversion of Oximes
into Amides The oxime (10mmol) and FeCl3 (30-40mmol) were mixed in a
mortar. The reaction mixture was allowed to stand at 80-90°C for 1.5-3 h.
The progress of reaction was followed by dissolving a sample in acetone
and monitoring on silica gel plates (SIL G/UV 254 Plates). Water (15 ml)
was added and the whole extracted with chloroform (3 x 20 ml). Drying and
evaporation of the solvent gave the products in 81-95% yields which
recrystallized from n-heptane. Table 1, Entry 8, yield 90%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid state, no solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Solvent free Beckmann rearrangement of ketoximes by anhydrous ferric
chloride
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
