$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of the Support To 100 g of SiO2
(70-230 mesh) : AlCl3 · 6H2O: ZnCl2 (5 : 2.3 : 1.28 w/w/w), was added
150mL of water and the product well mixed to give a gel-like material.
The water was evaporated in vacuo and the gel left to stand at 120°C
overnight. The resulting solid granules were ground and further activated
by heating to 230°C in vacuo. The catalyst was stored under dry
conditions. Beckmann Rearrangement (General Procedure) To a solution of
ketoxime (5 mmol) in dry CH2Cl2 (15 mL), 0.5 g catalyst was added. After
mixing well and the solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure. The
residue was subjected to microwave irradiation for the given time (Table
1). After the reaction course, the resulting mixture was extracted by
CH2Cl2 or acetone (2 x 10 mL), then filtered and the solvent was
evaporated. The residue was then recrystallized from a suitable solvent
(n-PrOH or EtOH). Products were known and gave satisfactory spectroscopic
data compared with those of authentic samples.[12] Table 1. Entry 4,
yield 93%. M.p. (°C) [Lit.]: 135-138 (137)[9] .
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, solid-supported catalyst, Beckmann reaction, microwave
irradn.in third stage, no solvent in third stage
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Solid-supported microwave-assisted Beckmann rearrangement of ketoximes in
dry media
