$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 5-Azepane-2-one Ethylene Ketal (2). Oxime 1 (60 mmol) was
dissolved in 170 mL of acetone in a 500 mL round-bottomed flask charged
with a magnetic stirrer. Addition of 60 mL of 4 N aqueous NaOH solution
was followed by slow addition of p-toluenesulfonoyl chloride (108 mmol)
dissolved in 170 mL of acetone. The reaction mixture was allowed to mix 2
h at room temperature. After the evaporation of acetone 40mL of H2O was
added. The reaction mixture was then neutralized by dropwise addition of
4 N aqueous HCl solution. The reaction was allowed to proceed overnight
at room temperature. The reaction mixture was transferred into an
extraction funnel, and the product was separated by extraction with
CH2Cl2 (5 x 200 mL). Combined organic phases were dried over anhydrous
Na2SO4 and filtered, and the solvent was evaporated. 5-Azepane-2-one
ethylene ketal, KLCL (9.6 g, 93%), was recrsytallized twice from acetone.
mp 104 °C. Anal. Calcd for C8H13NO3; C: 56.13 H: 7.65 N: 8.18. Found: C:
56.26 H: 7.71 N: 8.09. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm) = 7.7 (s, 1H),
3.7 (s, 4H), 3.0 (t, 2H), 2.3 (t, 2H), 1.6 (m, 4H). 13C NMR (75 MHz,
CDCl3): δ (ppm) = 178.3, 108.6, 64.0, 38.7, 37.0, 32.5, 30.3. IR (KBr): ν
3214 (s), 2967 (w), 2896 (w), 1664 (s), 1448 (m), 1114 (s), 896 (m) 507
(w) cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and Ring-Opening Polymerization of 5-Azepane-2-one Ethylene
Ketal: A New Route to Functional Aliphatic Polyamides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Tarkin-Tas, Eylem; Mathias, Lon J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Macromolecules (Washington, DC, United States) (2010), 43(2), 968-974

