$DATUM Synthesis of azepan-2-one (Table 3, entry 21). 15 To a solution of
cyclohexanone oxime (226 mg, 2 mmol in 5 mL acetonitrile) in a two-necked
flask equipped with reflux condenser under nitrogen atmosphere, was added
mercury(II) chloride (165 mg, 0.6 mmol). After being stirred at 80°C for
8 hr, the reaction mixture was allowed to cool and then acetonitrile (5
mL) was added to dissolve the solid formed. The solvent was stripped off
and the organic material was taken up in dichloromethane (4x10 mL). The
combined organic layers were washed with brine, dried over magnesium
sulphate, and filtered. The filtrate was evaporated under reduced
pressure and the residue obtained was purified by flash-column
chromatography over silica gel (230-400 mesh) with a
dichloromethane-methanol (100:4) eluent system to afford azepan- 2-one
(208 mg, 92%). mp 70-71°C. 1H NMR δH(400 MHz; CDCl3; Me4Si; 25°C) 7.46
(1H, br.s), 3.21-3.16 (2H, m), 2.45-2.40 (2H, m), 1.75-1.71 (2H, m),
1.68-1.62 (4H, m).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Mercury-Catalyzed Rearrangement of Ketoximes into Amides and Lactams in
Acetonitrile
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ramalingan, Chennan; Park, Yong-Tae
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2007), 72(12), 4536-4538

