$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of
2-Arylcarbamoyl-4-phenyl-1,3-selenazoles (8); General Procedure The
ketoxime 7 (5.0 mmol) was dissolved in anhyd Et2O (30 mL) and an excess
of PCl5 (3.00 g) was subsequently added. The mixture was refluxed with
stirring for 30 min. Et2O was removed by distillation and the residue was
washed with H2O and recrystallized from EtOH to give 8.
2-(4-Chlorophenylcarbamoyl)-4-phenyl-selenazole (8b) Yield: 92%,
colorless needles (EtOH). mp 198-199 °C. IR (KBr): 820 (s), 900 (m), 1056
(s), 1101 (m), 1190 (w), 1236 (m), 1401 (s), 1500 (s), 1536 (s), 1601
(s), 1691 (s), 3115 (m), 3382 (s) cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ=
7.35-7.95 (m, 9 H, ArH), 8.51 (s, 2JSeH = 45.6 Hz, 1 H, 5-H, Hetar), 9.10
(br s, 1 H, NH). 13C NMR (75 Hz, CDCl3): δ = 121.09 (5-C, Hetar), 125.65
(Ar), 126.68 (Ar), 128.62 (Ar), 128.92 (Ar), 129.26 (Ar), 129.86 (Ar),
134.50 (Ar), 135.65 (Ar), 157.37 (4-C, Hetar), 158.61 (2-C, Hetar),
170.59 (C=O). 77Se NMR (38.18 MHz, CDCl3, 60% Me2Se in CDCl3): δ =
766.97. MS (70 eV): m/z = 361 (35) [M+], 327 (5), 236 (7), 209 (12), 182
(11), 127 (5), 102 (100), 77 (5), 28 (2).Anal. Calcd for C16H11N2OClSe
(361.68): C, 53.14; H, 3.07; N, 7.74. Found: C, 53.21; H, 3.12; N, 7.95.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Beckmann rearrangement
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and reactivity of 2-acyl-1,3-selenazoles
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Geisler, Karlheinz; Kuenzler, Andreas; Below, Harald; Bulka, Ehrenfried;
Pfeiffer, Wolf-diethard; Langer, Peter
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2004), (1), 97-105

