$DATUM Synthesis of 7-tert-butylazepan-2-one (Table 3, entry 22). To a solution
of 2-tert-butylcyclohexanone oxime (339 mg, 2 mmol in 5 mL acetonitrile)
in a two-necked flask equipped with reflux condenser under nitrogen
atmosphere, was added mercury(II) chloride (165 mg, 0.6 mmol). After
being stirred at 80°C for 8 hr, the reaction mixture was allowed to cool
and then acetonitrile (5 mL) was added to dissolve the solid formed. The
solvent was stripped off and the organic material was taken up in
dichloromethane (4x10 mL). The combined organic layers were washed with
brine, dried over magnesium sulphate, and filtered. The filtrate was
evaporated under reduced pressure and the residue obtained was purified
by flash-column chromatography over silica gel (230-400 mesh) with a
dichloromethanemethanol (100:4) eluent system to afford
7-tert-butylazepan-2-one as a colorless oil (302 mg, 89%). 1H NMR δH(400
MHz; CDCl3; Me4Si; 25°C) 5.68 (1H, br.s), 3.03 (1H, dd, J = 9.54Hz;
6.02Hz), 2.52 (1H, dt, J = 2.19Hz; 12.80Hz), 2.45 – 2.40 (1H, m), 2.04 –
2.00 (1H, m), 1.97 – 1.92 (1H, m), 1.90 – 1.85 (1H, m), 1.60 – 1.45 (2H,
m), 1.27 – 1.18 (1H, m), 0.96 (9H, s).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Mercury-Catalyzed Rearrangement of Ketoximes into Amides and Lactams in
Acetonitrile
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ramalingan, Chennan; Park, Yong-Tae
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2007), 72(12), 4536-4538

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME144 STEP1
$RXN



